&lt;p&gt;###&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;12/24/2025&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Re: Core Botanica Storage Fire&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On December 23, 2025, at approximately 1915 hours, Crook County Fire and Rescue was dispatched for a fire at Core Botanica, on NW Lone Pine Road, in Crook County.&amp;nbsp; Initial reports were that a large fire was burning in a mint storage building at the facility.&amp;nbsp; Arriving crews discovered an approximately 36,000 square foot storage building fully involved.&amp;nbsp; It was determined the building was currently storing millions of pounds of shredded mint leaf, awaiting processing at the facility.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Crews set up defensive operations to protect other buildings on site.&amp;nbsp; No other buildings were damaged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cause of the fire was determined to be accidental, the result of the spontaneous combustion of wet mint, located inside one of the large storage bins.&amp;nbsp; Due to the large quantities of stored mint, the scene will continue to smoke for several days.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No injuries, and Crook County Fire and Rescue was assisted on scene by Redmond Fire and Rescue, and the Crook County Sheriff&rsquo;s Office.&lt;/p&gt;
